ls of PFCE typically indicate robust economic growth, driven by consumer demand.^Historical trends in PFCE, reflect the impact of inflation, interest rates, taxation policies, and global economic conditions on consumer spending.^Compare PFCE with other economic indicators such as GDP growth, inflation, and employment rates to get a comprehensive view of the economic situation."}],"related":[{"slug":"average-daily-electronic-toll-collection","title":"E-Toll Collections (Daily Avg)"},{"slug":"bank-credit-growth","title":"Bank Credit Growth"},{"slug":"capacity-utilisation","title":"Capacity Utilisation"},{"slug":"cement-production","title":"Cement Production"},{"slug":"crude-oil-price-indian-basket","title":"Crude Oil Price (Indian Basket)"},{"slug":"domestic-passenger-car-sales","title":"Domestic Passenger Car Sales"},{"slug":"domestic-tractor-sales","title":"Domestic Tractor Sales"},{"slug":"energy-requirements","title":"Energy Requirements"},{"slug":"essential-commodity-prices","title":"Essential Commodity Prices"},{"slug":"goods-and-services-tax-gst-collections","title":"GST Collections"},{"slug":"money-supply-m3","title":"Money Supply (M3)"},{"slug":"natural-gas-production","title":"Natural Gas Production"},{"slug":"non-oil-exports","title":"Non-Oil Exports"},{"slug":"petroleum-consumption","title":"Petroleum Consumption"},{"slug":"revenue-earnings-railway-freight-traffic-major-commodities","title":"Railway Freight Traffic- Revenue"},{"slug":"steel-consumption","title":"Steel Consumption"},{"slug":"steel-production","title":"Steel Production"},{"slug":"two-wheeler-sales","title":"Domestic Two-Wheeler Sales"}],"title":"Private Consumption (PFCE)","description":"India's private final consumption expenditure figure stands at 7.14% for Jun 2026. PFCE is typically the largest component of GDP by expenditure share.","headline":{"Absolute":"India's private final consumption expenditure figure stands at ₹ 44,742.8 Billion for Jun 2026. PFCE is typically the largest compon